{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q31153","formula":"Cl₃Ga","hill":"Cl3Ga","elements":["Cl","Ga"],"composition":{"Cl":3.0,"Ga":1.0},"names":{"en":"Gallium trichloride","ru":"Хлорид галлия(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Gallium(III) chloride is an inorganic chemical compound with the formula GaCl3 which forms a monohydrate, GaCl3·H2O. Solid gallium(III) chloride is a deliquescent with colorless crystals and exists as a dimer with the formula Ga2Cl6. It is colourless and soluble in virtually all solvents, even alkanes, which is unusual for a metal halide. It is the main precursor to most derivatives of gallium and a reagent in organic synthesis.","ru":"Хлорид галлия — бинарное неорганическое соединение, соль металла галлия и соляной кислоты с формулой GaCl3, белые гигроскопичные кристаллы, молекулы димерны, с водой образует кристаллогидрат."},"fame":24,"pubchemCid":26010,"mass":176.08,"charge":0,"smiles":"Cl[Ga](Cl)Cl","inchikey":"UPWPDUACHOATKO-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"trichlorogallane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-30952","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[12.141,0.0,0.0],[0.0,6.916,0.0],[-4.151,0.0,5.842]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.446,"y":0.0,"z":2.411,"el":"Ga"},{"x":2.446,"y":6.916,"z":2.411,"el":"Ga"},{"x":5.543,"y":0.0,"z":3.431,"el":"Ga"},{"x":5.543,"y":6.916,"z":3.431,"el":"Ga"},{"x":-2.076,"y":5.09,"z":2.921,"el":"Cl"},{"x":10.065,"y":5.09,"z":2.921,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-2.076,"y":1.826,"z":2.921,"el":"Cl"},{"x":10.065,"y":1.826,"z":2.921,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.996,"y":3.458,"z":1.941,"el":"Cl"},{"x":6.994,"y":3.458,"z":3.901,"el":"Cl"},{"x":5.993,"y":0.0,"z":5.491,"el":"Cl"},{"x":5.993,"y":6.916,"z":5.491,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.996,"y":0.0,"z":0.352,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.996,"y":6.916,"z":0.352,"el":"Cl"},{"x":8.517,"y":3.458,"z":2.411,"el":"Ga"},{"x":-0.527,"